IMPORTANT BEFORE DEPLOYMENT
1. Confirm contact@cineinsta.com is a real working mailbox/forwarder. Replace it in contact.html, privacy-policy.html, terms.html and disclaimer.html if a different address is used.
2. Deploy all five new HTML pages alongside index.html. Do not deploy index.html alone.
3. After deployment, open every footer link on desktop and mobile.
4. Verify /about.html, /contact.html, /privacy-policy.html, /terms.html and /disclaimer.html return real pages (not 404s).
5. Verify the homepage still loads the news feed, trailers, Buzz and reviews.
6. Verify the existing AdSense code is unchanged.
7. Check AdSense > Privacy & messaging and configure Google's consent message/CMP for EEA, UK and Switzerland traffic if required for the chosen ad setup.
8. Keep the news workflow original and useful: deduplicate, rewrite in Cineinsta's own words, add context/value, attribute/link to sources, and avoid publishing copied articles.
9. Keep navigation clear and working on mobile.
10. Do a final live-site crawl after deployment: links, images, feeds, videos, canonical URLs, robots.txt and sitemap.xml.

ADDITIONAL AD-SAFETY CHECKS
- Ads must not look like navigation, download buttons, article cards or video controls.
- Do not encourage users to click ads.
- Do not use pop-ups/pop-unders that interfere with navigation.
- Keep substantive editorial content ahead of/alongside ads; do not make pages primarily advertising.
- Do not alter AdSense ad code after Google provides it.

NOTE
The legal pages are general website-policy drafts, not legal advice. Review them against the actual Cineinsta services, analytics, advertising configuration and applicable laws before publishing.

11. Upload robots.txt and sitemap.xml to the site root and submit the sitemap in Google Search Console.
12. Keep ads.txt at the site root after confirming the publisher ID is the correct Cineinsta AdSense account.
13. In AdSense > Privacy & messaging, configure the required European regulations message/CMP if Cineinsta serves ads to users in the EEA, UK or Switzerland.
14. Do not treat this package as a guarantee of AdSense approval. Google evaluates the live site and can change policy requirements.
